----ENDF/B-VIII.0     MATERIAL 5                                     5 1451
----- THERMAL NEUTRON SCATTERING DATA                                5 1451
------ ENDF-6 FORMAT                                                 5 1451
                                                                     5 1451
 Temperatures (K)                                                    5 1451
 ---------------                                                     5 1451
   293.6 400 500 600 700 800 1000 1200 1400 1600                     5 1451
                                                                     5 1451
 History                                                             5 1451
 -------                                                             5 1451
                                                                     5 1451
 This evaluation was produced at Bettis Atomic Power Laboratory in   5 1451
 October 2016 using the LEAPR module of NJOY2012 [1]. The phonon     5 1451
 frequency distributions for H and Y in YH2 were calculated using    5 1451
 the MedeA materials simulation software [2] and the alpha and       5 1451
 beta mesh were optimized as described in Ref. 3.                    5 1451
                                                                     5 1451
 Theory                                                              5 1451
 ------                                                              5 1451
 YH2 has a fluorite type cubic crystal structure with the yttrium    5 1451
 atoms forming a face-centered cubic sub-lattice and the hydrogen    5 1451
 atoms situated in the tetrahedral interstices. The VASP ab initio   5 1451
 density functional theory and PHONON lattice dynamics codes were    5 1451
 used to calculate the phonon spectra for H and Y in YH2. The        5 1451
 calculated 0 K lattice parameter of a=5.2032 Angstroms agrees       5 1451
 with x-ray diffraction measurements at 90 K [4]. The calculated     5 1451
 heat capacity agrees with measurements [5] and the calculated       5 1451
 phonon spectra agrees with inelastic neutron scattering             5 1451
 measurements [6,7]. The total scattering cross sections for YH2     5 1451
 agree with measurements [8,9].                                      5 1451
                                                                     5 1451
